er a default. Only the exact opt-down value under the policies table opts the unwired reviewer down; a copy elsewhere or an unreadable declaration requires the reviewer, and the legacy record answers only when that key is absent. The hook answer is one of: the gate off; on with the unwired reviewer required; on with it warned; a mixed declaration; or an unreadable declaration, as IF-298 carries. They no longer read a declared line themselves and instead reach it through that answer.\"\"\"\n+module = \"project-trajectory/scripts/check_privacy.py;project-trajectory/scripts/kitlib/config.py\"\n+code_symbol = \"_first_declared_line;_load_process_toml;read_privacy_review;hook_policy_answer;policy_declaration\"\n+detail = \"\"\"All policy enforcers, including the agent layer, obtain a declared policy answer from one parsed representation. A privacy gate or reviewer declaration the parse holds outside `[policies]` reads as gate on and reviewer required, whatever its value or any direct or legacy declaration; a name inside a string declares nothing. An unreadable or unparseable declaration is a distinct outcome, never a default. Only the exact opt-down value directly under the policies table opts the unwired reviewer down; a copy elsewhere or an unreadable declaration requires the reviewer, and the legacy record answers only when that key is absent. The hook answer is one of: the gate off; on with the unwired reviewer required; on with it warned; a mixed declaration; or an unreadable declaration, as IF-298 carries. The hooks no longer read a declared line themselves and instead reach it through that answer.\"\"\"\n test_refs = \"(see TC-031)\"\n status = \"Approved\"\n component = \"CMP-007\"\n@@ -1559,8 +1559,8 @@ phase = 4\n [design.LLR-155]\n sr_refs = [\"SR-137\", \"SR-139\"]\n title = \"The config layer: one parse, declaration checks, one comparison\"\n-module = \"project-trajectory/scripts/agent_policy.py\"\n-code_symbol = \"process_config/config_conflicts/approval_through/human_holds\"\n+module = \"project-trajectory/scripts/agent_policy.py;project-trajectory/scripts/bootstrap.py\"\n+code_symbol = \"process_config/config_conflicts/approval_through/human_holds;_migrate_dial_key_name\"\n detail = \"\"\"The configuration layer parses the policy declaration once, reads a dial from that parse with its legacy declaration as fallback, and returns refusal text rather than raising for a duplicate declaration, a wrong-typed value or an out-of-range value. It supplies the ordinal approval level and the one comparison every consumer uses. Valid TOML syntax, including dotted keys, inline tables and multi-line strings, is not a refusal condition.\"\"\"\n rationale = \"\"\"The policy values serve several entry points, so their validation and comparison need one home. A duplicate or invalid declaration must surface as a refusal rather than letting each entry point choose a different fallback; valid TOML syntax is a parser concern, not a policy violation.\"\"\"\n test_refs = \"TC-150;TC-151\"\ndiff --git a/docs/requirements/system-requirements.toml b/docs/requirements/system-requirements.toml\nindex 80319a3c7..822354633 100644\n--- a/docs/requirements/system-requirements.toml\n+++ b/docs/requirements/system-requirements.toml\n@@ -214,7 +214,7 @@ boundary_refs = [\"B-05\"]\n hat_refs = [\"CONSISTENCY\", \"SECURITY\"]\n requirement = \"Every delivered enforcer of a declared policy dial shall read the same value for that dial as every other enforcer — one parse, one answer, across the hooks, the loop and the checkers alike.\"\n rationale = \"Realizes SN-028's one readable policy home. A policy answer calculated more than once can diverge across enforcers, leaving the owner unable to know which value governs; one parse gives every enforcer the same answer. SR-137 owns whether a declaration is ambiguous or invalid, while this row owns agreement among the enforcers that consume a valid declaration.\"\n-acceptance_criteria = \"Every enforcer reads the same value for the same dial from one TOML parse, including a dotted key, an inline table and a multi-line string; none refuses any of those valid TOML forms for its shape, and an unreadable declaration refuses rather than reading a default.\"\n+acceptance_criteria = \"Every enforcer reads the same value for the same dial from one TOML parse, including a dotted key, an inline table and a multi-line string; none refuses any of those valid TOML forms for its shape. A privacy gate or reviewer declaration outside `[policies]` reads as gate on and reviewer required for every enforcer, and an unreadable declaration refuses at the hooks rather than reading a default.\"\n priority = \"M\"\n verification = \"Test\"\n status = \"Approved\"\n@@ -485,9 +485,9 @@ title = \"One policy home with conflict and validity refusal\"\n sn_refs = [\"SN-028\"]\n boundary_refs = [\"B-01\", \"B-04\"]\n hat_refs = [\"CONSISTENCY\", \"SECURITY\"]\n-requirement = \"The kit shall read every process policy dial from a single policy declaration home and refuse an ambiguous or invalid declaration rather than resolve it by precedence or default.\"\n+requirement = \"The kit shall read every process policy dial from a single policy declaration home and refuse a duplicate declaration or a wrong-typed or out-of-range value rather than resolve it by precedence or default.\"\n rationale = \"A single declaration home gives the owner one place to inspect and change each dial. A duplicate declaration can give enforcers different values, and an invalid value can silently change a gate; refusing either condition keeps the owner in control instead of choosing an unrequested interpretation.\"\n-acceptance_criteria = \"\"\"A dial declared in both homes produces a refusal naming the key and both homes at every guarded entry point; a wrong-typed or out-of-range dial is refused rather than defaulted.\"\"\"\n+acceptance_criteria = \"\"\"A dial declared in both homes produces a refusal naming the key and both homes at the policy guard entry points; a wrong-typed or out-of-range dial is refused rather than defaulted.\"\"\"\n priority = \"S\"\n verification = \"Test\"\n status = \"Approved\"\ndiff --git a/docs/test/test-cases.toml b/docs/test/test-cases.toml\nindex bef78f3d6..898ccd90b 100644\n--- a/docs/test/test-cases.toml\n+++ b/docs/test/test-cases.toml\n@@ -333,11 +333,11 @@ phase = 1\n [test.TC-031]\n verifies = [\"SR-031\", \"LLR-031\", \"IF-037\"]\n level = \"Integration\"\n-method = \"\"\"Drive each shipped commit and push hook and the checker with a policy file containing a dotted key, an inline table, and a multi-line string. For each form, compare every policy answer with the TOML parser's answer and assert no hook or checker refuses the file for its shape. Drive an unreadable declaration and a mixed declaration through each hook; run the policy suites to confirm every enforcer reads one value per dial. Exercise the unwired-reviewer posture: only the exact opt-down value under the policies table warns, a copied value requires review, and the legacy record answers only when that key is absent. Inspect that no hook reads a declared line itself.\"\"\"\n+method = \"\"\"Drive each shipped commit and push hook and the checker with a policy file containing a dotted key, an inline table, and a multi-line string. For each form, compare every policy answer with the TOML parser's answer and assert no hook or checker refuses the file for its shape. Separately drive a privacy gate or reviewer declaration under another table and assert every reader, including the agent layer, reads gate on and reviewer required. Drive an unreadable declaration and a mixed declaration through each hook; run the policy suites to confirm every enforcer reads one value per dial. Exercise the unwired-reviewer posture: only the exact opt-down value under the policies table warns, a copied value requires review, and the legacy record answers only when that key is absent. Inspect that no hook reads a declared line itself.\"\"\"\n tier = \"Full\"\n expected = \"Satisfies SR-031 AcceptanceCriteria\"\n automated = \"Yes\"\n-evidence = \"tests/test_process_config.py::test_valid_toml_policy_shapes_reach_every_reader; tests/test_process_config.py::test_an_unreadable_policy_file_is_refused; tests/test_process_config.py::test_a_mixed_config_is_refused_by_name; tests/test_gate_policy.py; tests/test_push_policy.py; tests/test_pre_push_hook.py::test_the_review_posture_follows_the_one_parse; tests/test_shell_portability.py::test_no_hook_reads_the_policy_as_text\"\n+evidence = \"tests/test_process_config.py::test_valid_toml_policy_shapes_reach_every_reader; tests/test_process_config.py::test_a_privacy_key_under_another_table_fails_closed_in_every_reader; tests/test_process_config.py::test_an_unreadable_policy_file_is_refused; tests/test_process_config.py::test_every_hook_refuses_an_unreadable_policy_file; tests/test_process_config.py::test_a_mixed_config_is_refused_by_name; tests/test_process_config.py::test_every_hook_refuses_a_mixed_config_with_one_text; tests/test_gate_policy.py; tests/test_push_policy.py; tests/test_pre_push_hook.py::test_the_review_posture_follows_the_one_parse; tests/test_shell_portability.py::test_no_hook_reads_the_policy_as_text\"\n status = \"Approved\"\n phase = 1\n \n@@ -1495,7 +1495,7 @@ method = \"\"\"Run the process-config suite over a duplicated declaration, wrong-ty\n tier = \"Full\"\n expected = \"Satisfies SR-137 AcceptanceCriteria\"\n automated = \"Yes\"\n-evidence = \"tests/test_process_config.py::test_a_mixed_config_is_refused_by_name; tests/test_process_config.py::test_a_wrong_typed_dial_is_refused_not_defaulted; tests/test_process_config.py::test_an_out_of_range_dial_is_refused_not_defaulted; tests/test_process_config.py::test_every_guarded_entry_point_refuses_a_mixed_config; tests/test_process_config.py::test_valid_toml_policy_shapes_cause_no_configuration_refusal\"\n+evidence = \"tests/test_process_config.py::test_a_mixed_config_is_refuse