{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_20","type":"agent_message","text":"Reconciled the checkpoint spine against HEAD. No rows added or statuses changed.\n\n| Row / cell | Before | After | Why |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| SR-031 `acceptance_criteria` | “…an unreadable declaration refuses rather than reading a default.” | Adds fail-closed handling for privacy keys outside `[policies]` and scopes unreadable refusal “at the hooks.” | Matches the settled shared-parser and hook behavior. |\n| SR-137 `requirement` | “refuse an ambiguous or invalid declaration” | “refuse a duplicate declaration or a wrong-typed or out-of-range value” | Removes the obsolete broad/ambiguous wording. |\n| SR-137 `acceptance_criteria` | “…at every guarded entry point…” | “…at the policy guard entry points…” | Limits the claim to exercised policy guards. |\n| LLR-031 `module` | `\"…/check_privacy.py\"` | Adds `\"…/kitlib/config.py\"` | Covers the shared declaration reader’s back-link. |\n| LLR-031 `code_symbol` | `\"_first_declared_line;…;hook_policy_answer\"` | Adds `policy_declaration` | Covers its `Implements: SR-031, LLR-031` tag; preserves `_first_declared_line` first. |\n| LLR-031 `detail` | One parsed answer, unreadable/mixed outcomes, direct opt-down, legacy fallback, no hook text-read. | Adds agent-layer coverage; specifies fail-closed misplaced privacy-key semantics and string non-declarations; retains no hook text-read. | Captures settled code and the new fail-closed test. |\n| LLR-155 `module` | `\"…/agent_policy.py\"` | Adds `\"…/bootstrap.py\"` | Covers the existing bootstrap back-link. |\n| LLR-155 `code_symbol` | `\"process_config/config_conflicts/approval_through/human_holds\"` | Adds `_migrate_dial_key_name` | Covers that bootstrap implementation tag. |\n| IF-037 `data` | `\"TOML tables: attestation, policies, checks, build\"` | Adds privacy keys outside `[policies]` read as gate-on/review-required. | States the interface’s fail-closed reading. |\n| TC-031 `method` | Valid TOML shapes, unreadable/mixed declarations, reviewer posture, no text-read inspection. | Adds a separately driven misplaced privacy gate/reviewer declaration and agent-layer assertion. | Makes the fail-closed behavior directly testable. |\n| TC-031 `evidence` | Valid-shape, unreadable, mixed, suite, posture, and text-read tests. | Adds `test_a_privacy_key_under_another_table_fails_closed_in_every_reader`, plus every-hook unreadable/mixed nodes. | Every cited behavior now has settled test evidence. |\n| TC-150 `evidence` | Duplicate/type/range/configuration nodes. | Adds `test_a_malformed_dial_is_REFUSED_not_silently_defaulted`. | Covers the approval-rung malformed-dial case. |\n\nSN-028’s prior intent amendment remains unchanged at checkpoint. I judge it **MEANING**, not CLARITY: it retires an obligation premised on two grammar readers and policy-file line shape.\n\nBuilder-list reconciliation: confirmed items 1–11 and 13–16. Item 10 is represented by SR-031/LLR-031 rather than SR-137 because it is a fail-closed reading outcome, not duplicate/type/range refusal. Extended the list with LLR-155’s missing bootstrap carrier/symbol. Item 12 remains intentionally unencoded: the agent configuration layer and hooks disagree on mixed misplaced-key-plus-legacy presence.\n\nArms map:\n\n| LLR | Outcome / refusal / exemption | TC clause and evidence |\n|---|---|---|\n| LLR-031 | Valid dotted, inline, and multiline TOML forms are parser-read and not shape-refused. | TC-031 valid-form clause; `test_valid_toml_policy_shapes_reach_every_reader` |\n| LLR-031 | Misplaced privacy gate/reviewer key fails closed as gate-on/review-required; strings do not declare it. | TC-031 separate misplaced-key clause; `test_a_privacy_key_under_another_table_fails_closed_in_every_reader` |\n| LLR-031 | Unreadable policy declarations refuse at hooks; mixed declarations refuse. | TC-031 unreadable/mixed clause; `test_every_hook_refuses_an_unreadable_policy_file`, `test_every_hook_refuses_a_mixed_config_with_one_text` |\n| LLR-031 | Exact direct opt-down warns; copied/unreadable declarations require review; legacy applies only when absent. | TC-031 reviewer-posture clause; `test_the_review_posture_follows_the_one_parse` |\n| LLR-031 | Hooks do not read declared policy lines as text. | TC-031 inspection clause; `test_no_hook_reads_the_policy_as_text` |\n| LLR-155 | Duplicate, wrong-typed, and out-of-range declarations refuse; valid TOML shape is exempt from configuration refusal. | TC-150 method; `test_a_mixed_config_is_refused_by_name`, `test_a_wrong_typed_dial_is_refused_not_defaulted`, `test_an_out_of_range_dial_is_refused_not_defaulted`, `test_a_malformed_dial_is_REFUSED_not_silently_defaulted`, `test_valid_toml_policy_shapes_cause_no_configuration_refusal` |\n\nChecks run:\n\n- `check_trajectory.py --strict` — `clean (980 work item(s), 866 done (88%), 34 cancelled, graph acyclic)`; existing advisory warnings only.\n- `trace.py --strict` — `SN=31 SR=138 LLR=326 TC=353 orphans=0 integrity=0`; existing advisory warnings only.\n- Pytest intentionally skipped as directed.\n\nPerspective pass:\n\n- SECURITY: SR-031, LLR-031, TC-031 — privacy-key misplacement fails closed.\n- FIRST-RUN-ADOPTER: no new finding; valid TOML forms remain accepted.\n- CROSS-PLATFORM: SR-031/TC-031 — parser-defined TOML behavior avoids shell text-shape dependence.\n- MAINTAINER: LLR-031/LLR-155 — carrier coverage now matches implementation tags.\n- TEST-ENGINEER: TC-031/TC-150 — added exact settled test nodes.\n- UX-DESIGNER, UX-ENGINEER, ACCESSIBILITY: no rendered user surface.\n- PERFORMANCE: no material resource or timing change.\n- CONSISTENCY: SR-031, LLR-031, IF-037, TC-031 — aligned parser/fail-closed vocabulary.\n- INTEGRITY-RECOVERABILITY: no durable-write change in this scope.\n- PRODUCT-FITNESS: SN-028 remains the governing one-home policy need.\n\nUnsettled, intentionally not made into requirements: the bootstrap migration writer still locates some policy content by line shape, a